FPT L3+L2: prepare folded page tables for anonymous THP faults

The enhanced THP deposit allocates missing upper levels using the radix
allocator. This bypasses L3+L2 folding when a huge fault initializes an
L4 slot. Prepare the PMD with the FPT allocator before locking it, for
both private huge pages and the huge zero page.

Allocate the directory outside the page-table lock and recheck its
parent before publishing it. Publish the pointer and folded bit
together, keep the separate-table fallback, and recheck that the PMD is
empty under its lock before installing the huge entry.

